## 13. Fair use, and no other rights

These terms do not limit any rights You have under fair use, fair dealing or similar rules of law. They give You no other rights than those written here: no right is implied from the way the software is sold, shared or described, and You have no right to sublicense or transfer Your licence, except that someone who receives the software from You gets their own licence under section 3.

## 14. If something goes wrong

If You break these terms, the licences You were given end automatically. They are **reinstated** if You stop the breach and put things right within 30 days of the Licensor telling You in writing what is wrong (for example by publishing the Credit Notice or ending the sale). The first reinstatement is automatic and retroactive. If You break these terms again after being reinstated, Your licences end permanently unless the Licensor chooses to restore them in writing.

Copies that other people received from You in good faith keep their licence, because it comes from the Licensor (section 3). Their rights do not end because Your rights ended.

